      "severity": "critical",
      "confidence": "high",
      "title": "Deadlock between \u0060CheckoutService.Commit\u0060 and \u0060InventoryService.Reserve\u0060",
      "why": "Lock-order inversion on 2 locks \u00B7 2 threads in cycle \u00B7 10 threads waiting behind",
      "whatItMeans": "Two pieces of code take the same two locks in opposite order. Under load they eventually interleave: each grabs its first lock, then waits forever for the other\u0027s. Anything else that needs either lock queues behind them. The process won\u0027t recover without a restart.",
      "nextSteps": [
        "Restart the process (or recycle the app pool) to recover now. A deadlocked process doesn\u0027t heal on its own.",
        "Take the locks in one order everywhere: {{lock/0x222350a5dd0}} before {{lock/0x222350a5e40}}, as \u0060CheckoutService.Commit\u0060 does. \u0060InventoryService.Reserve\u0060 takes them the other way round.",
        "Or don\u0027t call out while holding a lock: \u0060CheckoutService.Commit\u0060 calls \u0060InventoryCache.TryReserve\u0060 while it holds {{lock/0x222350a5dd0}}."
